From: RG EDC
Subject: [PATCH] app: return to the RG EDC shell; open on a shelf or game

Upstream slot (GPL-3.0-or-later, https://github.com/slot-cfw/slot) is a
whole-device frontend: in host mode it can only quit through the power menu
(PowerOff ends in SimPlatform::poweroff(), exit 0), which on the RG Rotate is
reached through a power key that ROCKNIX keeps for suspend. RG EDC runs slot
from its own shell, so:

- Add "Back to RG EDC" as the last row of the main menu (Menu button). It
  flushes the resume state and saves like an eject, then takes the existing
  power-off path, which exits with status 0. In host mode the power-off
  screen reads "Back to RG EDC" instead of "Powering Down".
- SLOT_SHELF=gb|gbc|gba|recents|favorites opens slot on that shelf (rack
  keys as slot stores them), overriding the remembered shelf.
- SLOT_INSERT=<rom path or file name> selects that cart (by file stem, on
  the SLOT_SHELF shelf if given, otherwise any system shelf) and inserts it
  once the shelf is up, for "resume last game" from the shell.
- SLOT_BACK_EXITS=1 makes B on the shelf return to the shell too.

This patch is distributed under the same GPL-3.0-or-later licence.
